1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,415
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,509
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,559 --> 00:00:18,550
The Dragon Who Sneezed Soap Bubbles!

7
00:00:23,162 --> 00:00:28,793
Once upon a time, in Sunflower Village,
there lived a young dragon named

8
00:00:28,843 --> 00:00:30,090
Bartholomew.

9
00:00:30,483 --> 00:00:34,286
He was green-turquoise,
round, and very gentle.

10
00:00:34,979 --> 00:00:37,837
All the dragons learned to breathe fire.

11
00:00:38,021 --> 00:00:41,407
And that day, it was Bartholomew's turn.

12
00:00:42,105 --> 00:00:46,283
He filled his chest with air
and squeezed his eyes shut.

13
00:00:46,866 --> 00:00:47,846
Achoo!

14
00:00:47,896 --> 00:00:49,810
sneezed Bartholomew.

15
00:00:50,478 --> 00:00:51,761
Out of his nose came...

16
00:00:51,811 --> 00:00:53,225
a soap bubble!

17
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:56,167
A huge, round, shiny one.

18
00:00:56,393 --> 00:01:00,515
It floated up, up,
reflecting the blue sky.

19
00:01:00,714 --> 00:01:02,142
Then it went:

20
00:01:02,215 --> 00:01:03,415
pop!

21
00:01:03,758 --> 00:01:08,227
Up on a branch, Popcorn the
little owl flapped her wings.

22
00:01:08,786 --> 00:01:10,163
Hoo, hoo!

23
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:13,407
That bubble was almost
as big as a pumpkin!

24
00:01:13,457 --> 00:01:14,898
Popcorn said.

25
00:01:15,530 --> 00:01:17,625
But the other dragons giggled.

26
00:01:17,803 --> 00:01:20,120
Bartholomew lowered his nose.

27
00:01:20,337 --> 00:01:23,306
He wanted so much to
breathe fire like them!

28
00:01:24,402 --> 00:01:27,955
Bartholomew decided to try a
pepper to wake up his fire.

29
00:01:28,340 --> 00:01:30,143
He bit a little red one.

30
00:01:30,389 --> 00:01:34,677
His tongue, ears, and even
his tail tip felt hot!

31
00:01:35,259 --> 00:01:36,240
Achoo!

32
00:01:36,290 --> 00:01:38,203
sneezed Bartholomew.

33
00:01:38,933 --> 00:01:40,541
Bubbles flew out:

34
00:01:40,593 --> 00:01:42,854
pop, pop, pop.

35
00:01:43,065 --> 00:01:48,404
One landed on his horn, another slid
down his nose, and a third stuck to his

36
00:01:48,454 --> 00:01:49,654
tail.

37
00:01:50,013 --> 00:01:55,088
A girl named Mel was peeking over the
fence, with a little drawing notebook

38
00:01:55,138 --> 00:01:56,372
under her arm.

39
00:01:57,036 --> 00:01:59,331
Those bubbles are beautiful!

40
00:01:59,538 --> 00:02:00,704
How do you do that?

41
00:02:00,754 --> 00:02:02,056
Mel asked.

42
00:02:02,710 --> 00:02:06,249
Bartholomew blushed all the
way to the tip of his tail.

43
00:02:06,752 --> 00:02:08,547
I was trying to make fire,

44
00:02:08,597 --> 00:02:09,575
he explained.

45
00:02:09,625 --> 00:02:11,926
But this is what always comes out.

46
00:02:12,539 --> 00:02:14,064
Mel didn't laugh.

47
00:02:14,298 --> 00:02:16,378
She thought it was lovely.

48
00:02:17,043 --> 00:02:19,265
I think that's pretty special already,

49
00:02:19,315 --> 00:02:20,434
Mel said.

50
00:02:20,484 --> 00:02:23,029
Can I stay and watch your next try?

51
00:02:23,682 --> 00:02:26,638
Bartholomew nodded, very happy.

52
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:30,728
The next day, Mel came back with a plan:

53
00:02:30,778 --> 00:02:33,275
breathe, point, and blow.

54
00:02:33,486 --> 00:02:37,742
Bartholomew took a deep breath,
pointed at a pile of dry leaves...

55
00:02:37,792 --> 00:02:38,992
and blew.

56
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:40,480
Achoo!

57
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:42,444
sneezed Bartholomew.

58
00:02:43,117 --> 00:02:45,142
Pop, pop, pop!

59
00:02:45,421 --> 00:02:47,404
Bubbles covered the leaves.

60
00:02:47,598 --> 00:02:50,331
And one landed right on Popcorn's head.

61
00:02:50,523 --> 00:02:54,714
She looked cross-eyed, trying
to see her own soapy hat.

62
00:02:55,287 --> 00:02:56,663
Hoo, hoo!

63
00:02:56,778 --> 00:02:58,890
I'm wearing a see-through helmet!

64
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:00,381
Popcorn said.

65
00:03:01,009 --> 00:03:02,229
Mel giggled.

66
00:03:02,407 --> 00:03:04,877
And Bartholomew giggled, too.

67
00:03:05,534 --> 00:03:10,275
Just then, Granny Cotinha, the
oldest lady in the village,

68
00:03:10,325 --> 00:03:11,906
walked through the gate.

69
00:03:12,238 --> 00:03:15,819
She knew every tree and every bird.

70
00:03:16,463 --> 00:03:19,454
Bubbles like these don't
come along every day,

71
00:03:19,504 --> 00:03:21,163
Granny Cotinha said.

72
00:03:21,213 --> 00:03:25,916
It might be good to save some of that
surprise for when somebody needs it.

73
00:03:26,535 --> 00:03:29,671
Bartholomew thought about
that for the rest of the day.

74
00:03:30,779 --> 00:03:32,901
Then a heat wave arrived.

75
00:03:33,092 --> 00:03:37,992
The sun shone without stopping,
and the air felt like warm soup.

76
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:43,743
The flowers drooped, the well was nearly
empty, and everyone looked for a bit

77
00:03:43,793 --> 00:03:44,993
of shade.

78
00:03:45,441 --> 00:03:50,130
Hoo, hoo... my feathers feel
as warm as fresh-baked bread,

79
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:51,621
Popcorn said.

80
00:03:52,253 --> 00:03:54,361
Bartholomew looked at the well.

81
00:03:54,571 --> 00:03:56,165
He looked at the flowers.

82
00:03:56,403 --> 00:03:58,553
Then he looked at his own nose.

83
00:03:59,116 --> 00:04:00,739
My bubbles could help!

84
00:04:00,789 --> 00:04:02,439
Bartholomew said.

85
00:04:03,084 --> 00:04:04,817
Everyone went quiet.

86
00:04:05,013 --> 00:04:08,080
Bartholomew felt butterflies in his tummy.

87
00:04:08,287 --> 00:04:10,617
But Mel stood right beside him.

88
00:04:11,264 --> 00:04:12,881
Let's find out together,

89
00:04:12,931 --> 00:04:14,131
she said.

90
00:04:15,248 --> 00:04:18,398
Bartholomew's nose began to tickle.

91
00:04:19,062 --> 00:04:20,989
Shall we sneeze along with him?

92
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:23,064
Get your little nose ready...

93
00:04:23,479 --> 00:04:25,754
One... two... three...

94
00:04:26,392 --> 00:04:27,372
Achoo!

95
00:04:27,422 --> 00:04:29,336
sneezed Bartholomew.

96
00:04:30,009 --> 00:04:32,034
Pop, pop, pop!

97
00:04:32,242 --> 00:04:35,087
Shiny bubbles floated across the square.

98
00:04:35,250 --> 00:04:38,816
Inside each one was a
little puff of cool mist.

99
00:04:39,148 --> 00:04:44,895
When a bubble touched a forehead or a
paw, it left behind a chilly breeze.

100
00:04:45,242 --> 00:04:46,600
What a relief!

101
00:04:47,263 --> 00:04:49,483
Granny Cotinha smiled.

102
00:04:50,109 --> 00:04:53,563
A cool breeze like this is
better than a feather fan,

103
00:04:53,613 --> 00:04:54,813
she said.

104
00:04:55,864 --> 00:04:58,472
But the flowers were still thirsty.

105
00:04:59,162 --> 00:05:00,674
He aimed carefully.

106
00:05:00,962 --> 00:05:03,223
He sneezed out a big bubble.

107
00:05:03,393 --> 00:05:06,502
It rose a little and
burst over the daisies.

108
00:05:06,674 --> 00:05:07,701
Plink!

109
00:05:07,751 --> 00:05:10,804
A cool sprinkle fell onto the petals.

110
00:05:11,432 --> 00:05:14,110
Mel pointed toward the sunflowers.

111
00:05:14,311 --> 00:05:16,655
Bartholomew turned his nose.

112
00:05:16,846 --> 00:05:17,946
Achoo!

113
00:05:17,996 --> 00:05:20,021
Pop, pop, pop!

114
00:05:20,265 --> 00:05:23,026
The bubble shower
watered the whole garden.

115
00:05:23,696 --> 00:05:26,013
One flower lifted its head.

116
00:05:26,192 --> 00:05:27,537
Then another.

117
00:05:27,703 --> 00:05:29,200
And another!

118
00:05:29,847 --> 00:05:34,372
Popcorn flew through the bubbles, and
one stuck to the tip of each wing.

119
00:05:34,952 --> 00:05:36,329
Hoo, hoo!

120
00:05:36,439 --> 00:05:39,273
Now I'm an owl wearing soap mittens!

121
00:05:39,323 --> 00:05:40,765
Popcorn said.

122
00:05:41,401 --> 00:05:42,926
Everyone laughed.

123
00:05:43,123 --> 00:05:48,620
And Granny Cotinha laughed so hard
she had to put her hands on her knees.

124
00:05:49,239 --> 00:05:53,653
The dragons who had giggled before
came over, looking sheepish.

125
00:05:54,334 --> 00:05:56,289
They said sorry for laughing.

126
00:05:56,485 --> 00:05:59,982
And Bartholomew forgave
them with a great big smile.

127
00:06:01,047 --> 00:06:05,114
When the heat was over, the
village threw a bubble party.

128
00:06:05,803 --> 00:06:08,439
Granny Cotinha made lemonade.

129
00:06:08,630 --> 00:06:13,080
And Popcorn was in charge of counting
the bubbles, but she got distracted

130
00:06:13,130 --> 00:06:16,030
every time one floated near her beak.

131
00:06:16,608 --> 00:06:18,701
One, two, three...

132
00:06:19,036 --> 00:06:19,950
Hoo!

133
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,897
That one looks like a hat!

134
00:06:21,947 --> 00:06:23,597
Popcorn exclaimed.

135
00:06:24,252 --> 00:06:28,799
Bartholomew made big bubbles for children
to walk through and tiny ones for

136
00:06:28,849 --> 00:06:30,221
birds to follow.

137
00:06:30,583 --> 00:06:33,401
They shone blue, green, and gold:

138
00:06:33,451 --> 00:06:34,651
pop!

139
00:06:34,935 --> 00:06:37,379
Every dragon has their own way,

140
00:06:37,429 --> 00:06:39,090
Granny Cotinha said.

141
00:06:39,140 --> 00:06:42,452
And every way can do a
different kind of good.

142
00:06:43,058 --> 00:06:46,722
Bartholomew felt a warm
feeling in his chest.

143
00:06:47,068 --> 00:06:50,066
This time, it was not embarrassment.

144
00:06:50,244 --> 00:06:51,533
It was joy.

145
00:06:52,623 --> 00:06:55,662
In the late afternoon,
the party grew calm.

146
00:06:56,312 --> 00:06:59,879
Popcorn landed softly
on Bartholomew's head.

147
00:07:00,473 --> 00:07:04,215
Hoo, hoo... your bubbles
made the whole day better,

148
00:07:04,265 --> 00:07:05,707
Popcorn said.

149
00:07:06,269 --> 00:07:09,751
And you stayed by my side when I
thought I couldn't do anything right,

150
00:07:09,801 --> 00:07:11,534
Bartholomew replied.

151
00:07:12,168 --> 00:07:16,771
Mel opened her notebook and drew
Bartholomew in the middle of a cloud of

152
00:07:16,821 --> 00:07:18,401
colorful bubbles.

153
00:07:19,029 --> 00:07:21,176
Being different isn't a flaw,

154
00:07:21,226 --> 00:07:22,864
Granny Cotinha said.

155
00:07:22,914 --> 00:07:26,738
Sometimes it's exactly
the gift everyone needs.

156
00:07:27,369 --> 00:07:29,186
Bartholomew smiled.

157
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:31,389
He still couldn't breathe fire.

158
00:07:31,584 --> 00:07:35,540
But now he knew he didn't have to
be like everyone else to matter.

159
00:07:36,163 --> 00:07:40,216
That night, Sunflower
Village slept nice and cool.

160
00:07:40,528 --> 00:07:44,353
And Bartholomew fell asleep
peacefully, dreaming of bubbles...

161
00:07:44,403 --> 00:07:46,664
pop... pop... pop.

162
00:07:47,969 --> 00:07:49,169
The End.

163
00:07:50,876 --> 00:07:51,588
Hoo...

164
00:07:51,638 --> 00:07:52,662
Psst!

165
00:07:52,712 --> 00:07:54,284
Are you still awake?

166
00:07:54,438 --> 00:07:56,492
Did you like tonight's story?

167
00:07:56,621 --> 00:08:01,252
Bartholomew showed us that what makes
us different can be our superpower.

168
00:08:01,539 --> 00:08:03,762
Our differences are gifts.

169
00:08:03,901 --> 00:08:08,207
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

170
00:08:08,503 --> 00:08:13,401
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

171
00:08:13,451 --> 00:08:15,856
for more stories at bedtime.

172
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:17,360
Hoo...

